<section class="page">
  <h2>Training Module 2 — Machine Learning Systems</h2>
  <h3>Learning outcomes</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Supervised learning foundations:</strong> problem definition, loss functions, learning curves, training/test/validation sets, error analysis and metrics.</li>
    <li><strong>Classification:</strong> k-nearest neighbours, decision trees, random forests and support-vector machines.</li>
    <li><strong>Regression:</strong> linear methods, multiple regression, logistic regression and random forests.</li>
    <li><strong>Neural networks:</strong> TensorFlow development platforms, neural-network regression/classification, computer-vision applications and natural-language-processing applications.</li>
    <li><strong>Deployment:</strong> machine-learning system lifecycle, containers and APIs using Docker, and cloud services.</li>
    <li><strong>Limitations and ethics:</strong> appropriate use of learning techniques in decision-making systems, data/bias, uncertainty management and other ethical considerations.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Management, personal and social skills</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Select an appropriate learning model for a concrete problem.</li>
    <li>Develop and deploy a simple machine-learning application.</li>
    <li>Evaluate machine-learning systems from an ethical perspective.</li>
  </ul>
